course: dictionary
lesson: 13753
title: A big word for a talk
level: primary-6
stars: 2
explain: An interlocutor is a person you are talking with. It is a formal word, so you will mostly meet it in exam passages, news and history books. «My interlocutor on the phone was a patient lady who answered every question.» Here the interlocutor is the person on the other end of the call.
explain: Interlocutor can also mean a person or group who speaks for others in official talks, such as talks between countries. «The neutral country acted as the interlocutor between the two sides during the peace talks.» The clue is peace talks: the interlocutor carries the conversation for other people. Check by swapping in "the person I was talking to". It fits the first meaning, so you know which one is used.
explain: Context shows the tone. Words like official, serious, trusted or reliable near interlocutor tell you the talk is formal and important. «Both sides trusted her, so she was a reliable interlocutor.» Reliable means you can count on someone, so the interlocutor is a person people rely on.
fact: An interlocutor is a person you are talking with.
fact: In official talks between countries or groups, an interlocutor is a person or group who speaks on behalf of others.
fact: In old-style stage shows, the interlocutor was the person in the middle who asked the questions and led the jokes.
fact: Common phrases include «my interlocutor», «a reliable interlocutor» and «a trusted interlocutor».
fact: Interlocutor is a formal word; in everyday talk, people usually say "the person I was talking to".
exercise: What does interlocutor mean? | *The person you are talking with | A question nobody can answer | A telephone company
exercise: «The neutral country acted as the interlocutor between the two sides in the peace talks.» What job did the country do? | A shopkeeper selling food | A referee in a football match | A teacher marking a test | *A go-between who spoke for others in official talks
exercise: Which word is the formal word for the person you are talking with? | *interlocutor | cushion | biscuit | puddle
test: «In the old variety show, the interlocutor asked the questions and led the jokes.» What was the interlocutor's job in the show? | The stage lights operator | The man who sold the tickets | A singer who sang the songs | *The person in the middle who asked the questions
test: «She was a reliable interlocutor, and both sides trusted her to pass on every message.» What does reliable suggest about her? | She talked very loudly all the time | *She could be trusted to carry messages properly | She was always late | She never spoke at all
exam: «The two groups chose a trusted interlocutor to speak for them in the talks.» In your own words, what does the interlocutor do here? | Sells tickets to the public | Cooks the food for the meeting | *Speaks for the groups in the official talks | Locks the doors of the room
